libsmb2 for Snes9x PS5
======================

What:     libsmb2 from upstream master after 6.2 (no release has the fixes below yet), commit
          57fea04fd29403e3978000179339c8e13ce46b5c (2026-10-20, "libdcerpc: tests: schannel over the RPC
          layer"), the SMB 2/3 client library by Ronnie Sahlberg and contributors. Taken over 6.2 for its
          fixes of memory-safety bugs a malicious server can reach: CVE-2025-57632 (5e75eeb, heap OOB write
          in smb2_add_iovector via chained PDUs), CVE-2026-110712 (57bee9f, OOB read in
          smb2_decode_file_all_info), d0801c5 (off-by-one in the compat strdup), and the later "Bound ..."
          fixes (bf8d97d create/read/ioctl/notify replies, dd0bbde FILESYSTEM_INFO labels, a68698e ntlmssp,
          09424fa iovec skip loop, be408f4 and 4ace19a query-info encoders, 595d128 ntlm: hashes).
Licence:  LGPL-2.1 (LICENCE-LGPL-2.1.txt, COPYING). Statically linked into the app; the sources
          here are the complete corresponding source. Replace the files and rebuild to relink.
Source:   git archive of that commit from https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2
          (6.2 came from libsmb2_6.2+dfsg.orig.tar.gz in the Debian archive).
Kept:     lib/*.c and lib/*.h (the client; the server code that shares libsmb2.c comes with it),
          include/ (smb2/*.h, libsmb2-private.h, portable-endian.h, slist.h, asprintf.h).
          Share enumeration is lib/smb2-share-enum.c (include/smb2/libsmb2-share-enum.h); upstream moved
          the general DCE/RPC code (6.2's dcerpc*.c) into a separate libdcerpc, which is not needed here.
Left out: Kerberos (krb5-wrapper.c), SMB over QUIC (quic.c, needs Linux QUIC), SMB Direct (smbdirect.c,
          needs RDMA), Apple CommonCrypto AES (aes_apple.c/.h), libdcerpc, the other platforms' folders
          and makefiles, examples, tests, utils, CMake, packaging.
Changed:  nothing in lib/ or include/. config.h is ours (it replaces the CMake-generated one); it takes
          randomness from arc4random_buf (HAVE_ARC4RANDOM_BUF) on both the host and the console.
          On the console, libsmb2's fcntl() and getaddrinfo() calls reach netfs/netfs_shims_ps5.cpp
          through the link-time --wrap list (NETFS_WRAPPED_PS5 in ps5/Makefile).
Built by: ps5/Makefile (LIBSMB2_*), used by ps5/netfs/backend_smb.cpp.
Updating: replace lib/ and include/ from the new upstream commit (minus the files left out above), keep
          config.h (check upstream's cmake/config.h.cmake for new HAVE_* switches), then make -C ps5 test.
